        "original_id": "ab70770f-d97d-54f9-b158-d36ae9df3e24",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Istanbul, Turkey, Ayakapı, Sultanahmet Meydanı\n- Buildings: Gül Mosque, Hippodrome of Constantinople\n- Concepts: Eastern Orthodox church, mosque, Byzantine buildings, Ottoman conversion\n\nFacts:\n- The Gül Mosque in Istanbul, Turkey, is a former Eastern Orthodox church that was converted into a mosque by the Ottomans.\n- The Gül Mosque is in Ayakapı and is one of the most important surviving Byzantine buildings on Istanbul's historical peninsula.\n- The Hippodrome of Constantinople is today a square in Istanbul named Sultanahmet Meydanı, and only a few fragments of the original structure survive.",
